cientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone. Conscientious = reliability, stress resilience good, technical competence (weather, computer). Communication issues (tone). Might affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Decision quality good, attention good, but communication poor, egocentric, not willing to develop (adaptability). Concern for others positive for crew cooperation but egocentric contradictory.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as loner. Good problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to discuss all candidates before final. As first contribution, we can introduce candidate B strengths and concerns, and give provisional recommendation maybe B. Or we could start by covering candidate A. Since no prior discussion, we can start with candidate A. Provide recommendation maybe B? But need to reference discussion? Since none, we can just state our current recommendation and reasoning.\n\nLet's pick candidate B as leading because strong reliability, stress, technical, but communication concerns moderate. Compare with A's unfriendly. B seems better overall.\n\nThus: I recommend Candidate B. Provide evidence: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Concern: pretentious, wrong tone (crew cooperation). But overall stronger than others.\n\nProvide METADATA_JSON vote B.\n\nProceed."}
